:: Widget Manor Alarm [widget]

<<widget "manoralarm_text">>
	<<if $manoralarm gte 40>>
		<span class="red">Security are on high alert.</span>
	<<elseif $manoralarm gte 20>>
		<span class="purple">Security are aware of an intruder.</span>
	<<elseif $manoralarm gte 10>>
		<span class="lblue">Security are suspicious.</span>
	<<else>>
		<span class="green">Security are relaxed.</span>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

:: Manor Heist Sit
<<effects>>

Landry smiles at you as you sit in the plushy booth seat. 
<br><br>

"Thanks for hearing me out. You're obviously pretty adept at finding what you need to survive, and I could use somebody with those kinds of skills."
<br><br>

Landry continues, "There is someone who owes me something. What it is isn't important, what matters is that they know not to mess with me.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube
<<effects>>

"They live on Danube street. Big fancy house, chances are you've seen it. Now, I don't care what you steal, but you've got to make it hurt. Make them regret messing with me, got it?" 
<br><br>

<<He>> slips you a scrap of paper with a hastily scribbled address on it. "Burn that. Oh, and if you get caught, you don't know me, right?"
<br><br>

You nod before Landry slips away in the hubbub of the Pub.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Pub]]>><<set $manorheist to 1>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Refuse
<<effects>>

You ignore Landry and leave through the front door.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Harvest Street]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Search
<<effects>>
<<unset $manorsearch>>

You stroll the streets, keeping an eye out for the address Landry gave you. 
<br><br>

It doesn't take long to find it, as it stands out quite a bit. A large resplendent Manor resting on a small hill, you aren't even sure if you needed the address. You toss the paper in a bin as you examine the Manor from the roadside, your keen eyes noting the many entrances and exits. Most apparent to you is the crumbled bit of perimeter wall, hidden from view by a swath of trees.
<br><br>

You approach the portion of wall slowly, keeping an eye out for any sort of prevention method set up. 
<br><br>

The way is clear, and you arrive at the wall with little problem. The broken wall is much lower than the rest of the barrier, and you are able to reach the edge without much difficulty.
<br><br>

<<link [[Climb over the edge|Manor Heist Danube Climb]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Manor Heist Danube Leave]]>><<set $manorsearch to 1>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Climb
<<effects>>

You grasp the edge of the wall, pulling yourself up onto the edge before throwing your legs over the side and sliding off the side.
<br><br>

<<if $worn.feet.type.includes("heels") and $feetskill lte 400>>

    You hit the ground hard, feeling your heeled feet twist below you as you tumble to the ground painfully.<<pain 10>><<gpain>>
    <br><br>

<<else>>

    You land gracefully on the other side, crouching low to absorb the impact.
    <br><br>
<</if>>

<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>>
<<if $danger gte (9900 - $allure)>>
    <<beastNEWinit 1 dog>>

        You stand up, brushing the dirt off of you, when you hear a bark. You look up just in time for the guard <<beasttype>> to collide with you, knocking you to the ground.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Dog]]>><<set $molestationstart to 1>><</link>>

    <<else>>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Climb 2]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Climb 2
<<effects>>
<<set $manoralarm to 1>>

<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

Quickly scanning for cover, you sneak closer to a shrub you can hide behind. Scanning the Manor grounds, everything seems clear. You quickly cross the grounds, pressing your body against the side of the Manor as you peek carefully through the window. 
<br><br>

The coast seems clear, so you carefully open the window and slip inside, finding yourself standing in a spacious dining room.You seem to be alone, but you're not sure how long it will stay that way.
<br><br>

<<link [[Search the room|Manor Heist Danube Search In]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Explore the manor|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Search In
<<effects>>

<<if $rng gte 51>>

    You search the room for any valuable items, rifling through drawers as quietly as you can.
    <br><br>

    Despite your extensive searching, you fail to find anything worth taking.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><</link>>
	<br>

<<else>>

    You search the room, searching quickly but quietly through the cabinet drawers. 
    <br><br>

    You find a collectible spoon. You figure it could be worth something.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Take it|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><<set $blackmoney += 15>><<crimeup 15>><</link>><<crime>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Leave it|Manor Heist Danube Search In Leave]]>><</link>>
	<br>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Search In Leave
<<effects>>

You leave the spoon. It would be cruel to ruin with their collection.

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Explore
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

You move to the breezeway leading to the great hall, carefully checking for any staff. 
<br><br>

The coast is clear, and you quickly step into the great hall.
<br><br>

<<if $landrytreasure is 1>>

    You have what you came for.
    <br><br>

     <<if $manoralarm lte 30>>

        <<link [[Leave through the dining room|Manor Heist Danube Leave Dining]]>><</link>>
         <br>

    <</if>>

    <<link [[Leave through the main door|Manor Heist Danube Leave Main]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    <<if $upchecked isnot 1>>

        <<link [[Go upstairs|Manor Heist Danube Up]]>><</link>>
        <br>
        
    <<else>>

        <<link [[Go upstairs|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><</link>>
        <br>

    <</if>>

    <<if $manorkitchen isnot 1>>

        <<link [[Search the rest of the lower floor|Manor Heist Danube Lower]]>><</link>>

    <</if>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

You decide to search the rest of the lower floor. Making your way carefully between rooms, you head to the back of the Manor. You're walking down a hall near the Kitchens when you hear footsteps approaching.
<br><br>

<<link [[Hide|Manor Heist Danube Lower Hide]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Hide
<<effects>>

The steps fade, and you take a deep breath before stepping back out into the hall.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen
<<effects>>
<<generate1>><<person1>>
<<unset $manorkitchen>>

<<set $danger to random(1,10000)>>
<<if $danger gte 8000 - (50 * [$manoralarm])>>

    You turn a corner, bumping directly into a servant. 
    <br><br>

    They fall to the floor, a platter of food crashing to the floor.<<gsuspicion>>
    <br><br>

    You run before <<he>> can get a good look at you.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You continue down the hallway until you reach an open doorway. Carefully peeking in, you discover that you are in the kitchen. The staff hurry around, flitting from appliance to appliance. You step into the kitchen carefully, ready to duck out of sight, but before you can move you are nearly bowled over. Turning around, you see an incredibly muscular <<personsimple>>.
    <br><br>

    Holding a massive cooking pot, <<he>> fix you with a firm stare. "Move."
    <br><br>

    You scurry out of the way as the <<personsimple>> flings open an oven door, throwing the pot inside and closing it firmly. Without a word <<personsimple>> turns and leaves.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><</link>>

<</if>>


:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

 With no one apprehending you, you take a moment to observe your surroundings and plan your next move.
<br><br>

You don't dare try to steal under the watchful eye of the head chef. Looking around, you see a thick door that could only lead to the cellar.
<br><br>

<<if $landrytreasure isnot 1>>

    <<link [[Enter the cellar|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar]]>><</link>>
     <br>

<</if>>

<<link [[Go back the way you came|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><<set $manorkitchen to 1>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar
<<effects>>

You wait for a moment of calm before quickly dashing towards the cellar door. No one seems to care that you are there, most likely assuming that you are related to some staff. With a quick step you open the cellar door enough to slip in and shut it behind you. You take a deep breath before descending down the stairs. 
<br><br>

At the bottom you emerge into a dimly lit room, illuminated only by a single hanging bulb. In the center of a room a small chest sits on a pedestal, mounted to the floor. Upon closer inspection, you see the chest itself has been bolted to the pedestal, preventing it from being removed.
<br><br>

You examine the latch, noting the extra thick lock that holds it shut. It's not like any lock you've seen before.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar 2]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar 2
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

Whatever is inside must be valuable, or they wouldn't go through such lengths to protect it.
<br><br>

<<link [[Pick the lock|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Pick]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Smash the lock|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Smash]]>><<set $manoralarm += 10>><</link>><<gsuspicion>>
<br>

<<if $cellarkey is 1>>

    <<link [[Use the key|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Key]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Pick
<<effects>>

You take the lock in your hands, feeling the heft of it. With slow careful attempts you try to get the lock to open, but it remains stubbornly locked. No matter which angle you try you can't seem to pick it. Frustrated, you let go of the lock.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar 2]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Smash
<<effects>>

You look around for something heavy to smash the lock. Hidden in the corner, you find a large marble sculpture. Taking it into your hands, you examine it closer. The bust is shaped like an arm, with a closed fist.
<br><br>

You return to the lock. Grasping the bust tightly, you raise it above your head and bring it down on the lock. The sound of the bust hitting the lock reverberates in the small room, but you raise it once more.
<br><br>

With a decisive strike you smash the lock once more, shattering the casing and knocking it to the floor. Before you can do anything, however, the entire podium begins to tilt. The impact of the bust must have knocked the mounting loose. With a resounding crash it falls to the floor. <<ggsuspicion>>
<<set $manoralarm += 30>>
<br><br>

You step around the toppled podium, bending over to see the contents of the now broken open box.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Safe]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Key
<<effects>>

You take the lock in your hands, feeling the heft of it. Inserting the Key, you turn it with a heavy "clunk."
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Safe]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Lower Cellar Safe
<<effects>>

<<switch random(1,4)>>

    <<case 1>>

        You peer into the box. 
        <br><br>

        The inside is lined with velvet, and sitting in the middle of the box is a large jewel encrusted phallic shaped object. The assortment of jewels are blindingly shiny. You quickly grab it, hastily leaving the room and re-entering the Kitchen.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 2>>

        You peer into the box. 
        <br><br>

        The inside is lined with velvet, and sitting in the middle is a small black box. You reach inside and pull it out, opening it carefully. Nestled inside there is a golden ring with a large, shiny diamond mounted on top. Looking closely, you notice "For M" engraved on the side. You quickly pocket the ring, and hastily retreat back to the Kitchen.
        <br><br>
        
        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 3>>

        You peer into the box. 
        <br><br>

        The inside is lined with velvet, and sitting inside is a large sheaf of paperwork. Taking it into your hands, you notice the elegant font at the top declaring "Deed of Conveyance." Looking closer, you see that it is the deed to a patch of land somewhere you don't recognize. You carefully fold up the paper before swiftly exiting back towards the Kitchen.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 4>>

        You peer into the box. 
        <br><br>

        The inside is lined with velvet, but nothing is inside. The box is completely empty. You stand up, empty-handed, and walk back to the Kitchen.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Lower Kitchen 2]]>><</link>>

<</switch>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up
<<effects>>
<<unset $bedroomchecked>>
<<unset $officechecked>>

You decide to explore the upper floor of the Manor. 
<br><br>

As you arrive at the top of the large staircase, you hear footsteps approaching. Looking around you duck into the closest room.You quickly scan your surroundings. 
<br><br>

It's a broom closet. Heart pounding, you stand by the door as you hear footsteps drawing closer. Through the door, you can hear muffled talking. 
<br><br>

"Inside… <span class="yellow">valuable</span>… Master." Before you can hear the rest, the footsteps fade.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 2]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up 2
<<effects>>

<<set $danger to random(1,10000)>>
<<if $danger gte 8000 - (50 * [$manoralarm])>>

    A servant steps out of a room, yelping in surprise as they see you. They break into a run, coming towards you. Thinking quickly, you jump onto the bannister of the grand staircase and let gravity slide you down to the lower floor. That was fun!<<lstress>><<stress -10>>
    <br><br>

    You reach the bottom floor and hide out of sight of the top of the stairs. The servant stops at the top, looking for you. "Shit, lost them. Gotta tell the Head…"<<gsuspicion>>
    <br><br>

    Once the footsteps fade you make your way back upstairs.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $manoralrm += 10>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You step out of the closet back onto the landing.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $upchecked to 1>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up 3
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

You're standing on the landing of the second floor. You can hear movement in the rooms around you, but you aren't sure where exactly it is coming from.
<br><br>

<<if $landrytreasure is 1>>

    You have what you came for. Time to escape
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Go downstairs|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><</link>>


<<else>>

    <<if $bedroomchecked isnot 1>>

        <<link [[Check the Bedroom|Manor Heist Danube Up Room]]>><</link>>
        <br>

    <</if>>

    <<if $officechecked isnot 1>>

        <<link [[Check the Office|Manor Heist Danube Up Office]]>><</link>>
        <br>

    <</if>>

    <<if $drawingchecked isnot 1>>

        <<link [[Check the Drawing Room|Manor Heist Danube Up DrawRoom]]>><</link>>
        <br>

    <</if>>

    <<link [[Go downstairs|Manor Heist Danube Explore]]>><</link>>

<</if>>



:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

<<if $manoralarm gte 20>>

    You approach the door with the "Master Suite" plaque affixed to it. The handle refuses to turn in your hand. It's locked.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Pick the lock|Manor Heist Danube Up Pick]]>><<set $manoralarm += 10>><</link>><<gsuspicion>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Leave|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Leave]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You approach the door with the "Master Suite" plaque affixed to it. The handle turns in your hand. It's unlocked.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 2]]>><</link>> 
    <br>
    <<link [[Leave|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room 2
<<effects>>
<<unset $safecode>>

<<set $danger to random(1,10000)>>
<<if $danger gte 8000 - (50 * [$manoralarm])>>

    You open the door and start to step in when you hear a noise from within. Stepping back, you press yourself against the wall and listen in.
    <br><br>

    The servant inside continues to clean the room, unaware of your presence. "Have to remember the Masters code… XXXX… Cannot forget…" The servant continues muttering as they finish cleaning. You hide behind the door as they leave, and slip in before the door closes. 
    <br><br>

    <span class="yellow">You now have the Bedroom safe code!</span>
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><<set $safecode to 1>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You look around, shocked at the display of wealth. The floors are an intricate marbled pattern, and the walls seem to be made of gold. The bed sits squarely in the center of the room, the 4 posts adorned with delicate silk sheets. You rub the sheets between your fingers, feeling a sense of longing.
    <br><br>

    Bailey would never let you have such nice sheets. Turning from the sheets, you see a large desk made of a dark wood. Your keen eye recognizes it as mahogany.
    <br><br>

    Underneath it, however, is the main focus. A large safe sits snugly beneath the desk, bolted to the floor. You crouch down for a better view. The safe is sturdily built, with no obvious way to pry it open. You'd need a code.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3
<<effects>>

You are stood in the Master Suite. Standing out to you is the mahogany desk and a stately dresser.
<br><br>

<<if $safecode isnot 1>>

    <<link [[Check the desk|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Desk]]>><</link>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Check the dresser|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Dress]]>><</link>>
    <br>

<</if>>

<<link [[Check the safe|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Safe]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room Desk
<<effects>>

<<if $rng gte 51>>

    You rifle through the drawers in the desk, not finding much. Not even a fancy pen to nick.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You rifle through the drawers in the desk, not finding much.
    <br><br>

    As you are about to close the final drawer, however, you notice a yellow piece of paper you had missed before. 
    <br><br>

    Scribbled on it is "Safe Code: XXXX." You place the paper back and close the drawer.
    <br><br>
    
    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><<set $safecode to 1>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room Dress
<<effects>>

<<if $rng gte 51>>

    You check the dresser, quickly rummaging through each drawer, but you come up empty. Not even a fancy tie to steal
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You check the dresser, quickly rummaging through each drawer, but you come up empty. 
    <br><br>

    As you search the last drawer you hear a crinkling noise. Pulling out a sock, you find a yellow piece of paper inside. Written on it is "Safe Code: XXXX." You put the paper back into the sock and close the drawer.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Safe]]>><<set $safecode to 1>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room Safe
<<effects>>

<<if $safecode is 1>>

    You crouch beside the safe, and reach out to enter the code. Firmly punching the numbers in, you wait as the safe emits a series of clicks and beeps. 
    <br><br>

    Finally, with a solid *click* it opens slightly. You grasp the door and pull it back.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room Safe 2]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You crouch down next to the safe. Without the code, there isn't much you can do.
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 3]]>><</link>>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room Safe 2
<<effects>>

<<switch random(1,4)>>

    <<case 1>>

        You swing open the safe door and look inside. 
        <br><br>

        Resting inside is a phallic shaped object, absolutely coated in precious gems. Even in the dim light underneath the desk it scatters the light in a dazzling array of colors. You pull it from the safe, closing the door. With a click, the lock reengages. Treasure in hand, you stand up and quickly leave the room.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $bedroomchecked to 1>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 2>>

        You swing open the safe door and look inside. 
        <br><br>

        Sitting inside is a small black box, the glimmer of velvet unmistakable. You take the box in your hand, surprised at the weight. With a small click you open the clamshell style box, revealing a large diamond ring nestled inside. The golden band is half buried in the velvet, and a massive diamond has been mounted on it. 
        <br><br>

        Looking closely, you notice "For M" has been engraved on the band. Treasure in hand, you place the box back inside the safe and close the door. With quick steps you leave the room.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $bedroomchecked to 1>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 3>>

        You swing open the safe door and look inside. 
        <br><br>

        Lying inside is a thick sheaf of paper, with "Deed Of Conveyance" emblazoned at the top in fancy script. Scanning the document, you realize it is the rights of ownership to a small patch of land. You don't recognize the address. With careful motions you fold up the paper and close the safe door. Standing, you make your way out of the Bedroom.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $bedroomchecked to 1>><<set $landrytreasure to 1>><</link>>

    <<case 4>>

        You swing open the safe door and look inside. 
        <br><br>

        Disappointingly, it is empty. You stand, empty-handed, and return to the landing.
        <br><br>

        <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><<set $bedroomchecked to 1>><</link>>

<</switch>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Pick
<<effects>>

You crouch down, looking closer at the locking mechanism. Despite how fancy the Manor is, it's a simple lock. Maybe even simpler than you would find in a regular house. It takes no time to unlock, and you slip in quietly. You go to lock the door, but find no way to lock it. It must only lock with a key. They'll know you were here
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Room 2]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Room Leave
<<effects>>

You leave the door be. You don't know if you could crack the lock anyways.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up 3]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Office
<<effects>>
<<unset $preypassword>>

You look around, impressed by the display of wealth. 
<br><br>

Standing center stage is a massive desk, made of a brushed metal you don't recognize. The only other things that stand out to you are the large and expensive looking computer on the desk, and an even larger painting on the wall behind the desk. The painting depicts a hawk swooping down and grabbing a terrified looking bunny. 
<br><br>

You turn from the painting and approach the desk.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Office 2]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Office 2
<<effects>>
<<manoralarm_text>>
<br><br>

The computer is on, and a flashing cursor asks for a password. You check through the desk, but can't find the password written down anywhere. Maybe you can guess the password.
<br><br>

<<link [[Try "Hunter"|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Hunter]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Try "Prey"|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Prey]]>><</link>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Office Hunter
<<effects>>

<<if $rng gte 51>>

    You type in "Hunter" and tap the accept key. 
    <br><br>

    The computer hums for a moment before it flashes red, refreshing the screen to a new one. "ERROR: Failed sign in. Notice sent to linked accounts" flashes on the top of the screen.<<gsuspicion>><<set $manoralarm += 10>>
    <br><br>

    You unplug the computer, then plug it back in. It hums for a moment, then returns to the sign in page
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Fail]]>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You type in "Hunter," and tap the accept key. 
    <br><br>

    The computer hums for a moment before it flashes white, refreshing the screen to a new one. It's a control panel, but only 2 options are available. One box flashes red, "OPEN WALL SAFE" written on it. The other flashes green, "SIGN OUT" written on it
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Choose to open wall safe|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Safe]]>><</link>>
    <br>
    <<link [[Choose to sign out|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Out]]>><</link>>
    <br>

<</if>>

:: Manor Heist Danube Up Office Prey
<<effects>>

<<if $rng gte 51>>

    You type in "Prey" and tap the accept key. 
    <br><br>

    The computer hums for a moment before it flashes red, refreshing the screen to a new one. "ERROR: Failed sign in. Notice sent to linked accounts" flashes on the top of the screen.<<gsuspicion>><<set $manoralarm += 10>>
    <br><br>

    You unplug the computer, then plug it back in. It hums for a moment, then returns to the sign in page
    <br><br>

    <<link [[Next|Manor Heist Danube Up Office Fail]]>><<set $preypassword to 1>><</link>>

<<else>>

    You type in "Prey," and tap the accept key. 
    <br><br>

    The computer hums for a moment before it flashes white, refreshing the screen to a new one. It's a control panel, but only 2 options are available. One box flashes red, "OPEN WALL SAFE" written on it. The other flashes green, "SIGN OUT" written on it
    <br><br>

